.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_CREATE_MPQE 3 2026-09-04 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_create_mpqe \- create an MPQE-wrapped MPQ archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.PP
.B int32_t libmpq__archive_create_mpqe(mpq_archive_s **archive, const char *path, const uint8_t *authentication_code, size_t authentication_code_size, const mpq_archive_create_options_s *options);
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a new MPQE stream containing an MPQ v1 or v2 archive. The caller
supplies at least 32 authentication-code bytes. The normal writer first
finalizes a private temporary MPQ, then encrypts it and atomically publishes
the result when
.BR libmpq__archive_close (3)
succeeds.
.PP
Existing MPQE archives cannot be modified. Creation uses temporary plaintext
storage in the destination directory. That temporary file is owner-only; the
completed MPQE archive uses normal output permissions determined by the
caller's umask. Cleanup is best effort, so a crash can leave an owner-only
plaintext temporary file behind.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success or a negative LIBMPQ_ERROR_* code. Missing or short
authentication data returns LIBMPQ_ERROR_DECRYPT.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__archive_create (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_open_mpqe (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_close (3)
